{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>נוקש</b> — a verb whose root is with [the letters] nun and vav [i.e., נקש]. The correct reading is kamatz katan under a pataḥ, for all the vowels are interchangeable. And its being from the conjugation of Targum [Aramaic] has no reason, for do we not find וינקשו מבקשי נפשי (and those who seek my soul were ensnared) — and behold, there are two roots." "<b>הגיון</b> — this I will recount in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:46.935927749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}